The warp-level reduction for summing `res` across all threads in a warp:

```cpp
// Warp shuffle reduction (butterfly pattern)
res += shift_left(res, 1);   // sum pairs:     lanes (0,1), (2,3), ...
res += shift_left(res, 2);   // sum quads:     lanes (0-3), (4-7), ...
res += shift_left(res, 4);   // sum octets:    lanes (0-7), (8-15), ...
res += shift_left(res, 8);   // sum 16-groups: lanes (0-15), (16-31), ...
res += shift_left(res, 16);  // sum 32-groups: lanes (0-31), (32-63) if warpSize=64
if(warpSize > 32)
    res += shift_left(res, 32); // sum full 64-wide warp (GFX9 only)

// Store warp result to LDS (only lane 0 of each warp)
if(tx % warpSize == 0)
    sdata[tx / warpSize] = res;
__syncthreads();

// Final reduction across warps (done by thread 0)
if(tx == 0)
{
    for(I k = 1; k < NB_X / warpSize; k++)
        res += sdata[k];
    sdata[0] = res;  // broadcast result
}
__syncthreads();
```

This handles both architectures: RDNA (warpSize=32) stops at shift 16, GFX9 (warpSize=64) adds shift 32.

