Key difference: Complex variants

Real (sgesvdj, dgesvdj):
- A, U, V, abstol, residual, S: All same type (float or double)

Complex (cgesvdj, zgesvdj):
- A, U, V: Complex (rocblas_float_complex or rocblas_double_complex)
- S, abstol, residual: REAL (float or double)
- Singular values always real (by definition)
- Tolerances and residuals are real norms

Why abstol/residual real for complex?
- Singular values are always real: ||A||_2 = max(S)
- Residual is Frobenius norm: ||off-diag||_F (real value)
- Tolerance compares real quantities
- Makes no sense to have complex tolerance

